From: McKernel native Rust integration
Subject: [PATCH] driver core: export existing device hotplug transaction APIs

The Rust IHK CPU adapter must hold device_hotplug_lock across the complete
multi-CPU preflight, transitions, final observations and compensation. The
exported add_cpu/remove_cpu wrappers take this mutex internally and cannot be
called while that batch lock is held. Export the existing lock and device
transition entry points without introducing a project C bridge or changing
their implementation. Callers retain device references and obey the existing
documented lock order. CPUHP policy callbacks separately protect reservations
between transactions.

--- a/drivers/base/core.c
+++ b/drivers/base/core.c
@@ -2344,11 +2344,13 @@ void lock_device_hotplug(void)
 {
 	mutex_lock(&device_hotplug_lock);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(lock_device_hotplug);
 
 void unlock_device_hotplug(void)
 {
 	mutex_unlock(&device_hotplug_lock);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(unlock_device_hotplug);
 
 int lock_device_hotplug_sysfs(void)
 {
@@ -4204,6 +4206,7 @@ int device_offline(struct device *dev)
 
 	return ret;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(device_offline);
 
 /**
  * device_online - Put the device back online after successful device_offline().
@@ -4235,6 +4238,7 @@ int device_online(struct device *dev)
 
 	return ret;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(device_online);
 
 struct root_device {
 	struct device dev;
